> Note that this ring
> increases your hunger by 50%, so have plenty of food when you use it.

Delete.  New/bad players already have a tendency to massively overvalue 
nutrition, and this advice will only make things worse.  In my time here 
and in Freenode #nethack, I've noticed that some players love =SD and 
horns of plenty, and hate =conflict, =regen, jumping, forced teleport -- 
all for nutrition considerations.  I've even seen people warn against 
overuse of ordinary rings, because of the extra 5% food consumption.

The truth is that if you spend your first 10k turns wearing rings of 
conflict and regeneration, plus any amulet, you'll use 21.5k nutrition... 
and get (my very rough estimate) 50k+ nutrition just from proceeding 
promptly through levels and eating every safe corpse and food item.

